---
// Privacy Policy. Written for Ghana's Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843).
// TODO before launch: have a lawyer review this, register with the Data
// Protection Commission, and fill in SITE.legalName, address and contacts.
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { prettyPhone } from '../lib/format';

const sections = [
  { id: 'who', title: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'use', title: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'share', title: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'location', title: 'Your location' },
  { id: 'storage', title: 'Cookies and device storage' },
  { id: 'keep', title: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'Keeping it safe' },
  { id: 'rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'children', title: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact us' },
];
---

<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" sections={sections} icon="shield" heading="How Relax&Bite protects your data">
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal information {SITE.name} collects when you use our app and website, why we
    collect it, who we share it with and the choices you have. We follow the Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843) of
    Ghana.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.legalName} ("{SITE.name}", "we", "us") runs a food ordering service that connects customers with
    restaurants, chop bars and delivery riders, starting in {SITE.area}. We are responsible for the personal
    information described in this policy. Our address is {SITE.address}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you order</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your email address</strong>, used to sign you in (with a one-time code or through Google). If you sign in with Google we receive your name and email address from Google, nothing else.</li>
    <li><strong>Your phone number</strong>, given at checkout so the restaurant and rider can contact you about your order.</li>
    <li><strong>Your name</strong>, if you give it, so the restaurant and rider know who the order is for.</li>
    <li><strong>Delivery details</strong>: your town, landmark, house number or GhanaPost GPS address, and delivery notes.</li>
    <li><strong>Your location</strong>, only if you allow it (see "Your location" below).</li>
    <li><strong>Orders</strong>: what you ordered, from whom, when, the amount and how you paid.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment details</strong>: payments are handled by our payment provider, Paystack. We receive a payment reference and the result. We never see or store your card number or Mobile Money PIN.</li>
    <li><strong>Reports and messages</strong> you send us, such as a problem with an order, and any photos you add.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage information</strong>: pages and restaurants viewed, items added to your bag, device and browser type, and a random visitor number stored on your device.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>When you join as a restaurant or rider</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, phone number and password (stored only in scrambled form). Your phone number is also how you sign in.</li>
    <li>For restaurants: business name, address, town, opening hours, menu and photos.</li>
    <li>For riders: Ghana Card number and photo, a passport-size photo, vehicle type and number plate, and an emergency contact.</li>
    <li>Payout details, such as a Mobile Money number or bank account, so we can pay you.</li>
    <li>Sales, deliveries and earnings records.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To take your order, pass it to the restaurant, arrange delivery and keep you updated.</li>
    <li>To sign you in with a one-time email code or with Google, and to email order alerts to restaurants and riders.</li>
    <li>To keep everyone safe: the 4-digit delivery code, showing you your rider's name and photo, checking riders' Ghana Cards, and investigating reports.</li>
    <li>To prevent fraud and fake orders, for example by limiting cash on delivery.</li>
    <li>To answer your questions, handle refunds and resolve complaints.</li>
    <li>To give restaurants and riders reports on their sales and visits. These reports show totals, not who you are.</li>
    <li>To understand how the service is used and make it better.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal, tax and accounting duties.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We send you service messages about your orders. We will only send you offers and promotions if you agree, and you
    can stop them at any time.
  </p>

  <h2 id="share">Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The restaurant</strong> you order from receives your name, phone number and order.</li>
    <li><strong>Your rider</strong> receives your name, phone number, delivery address, landmark and notes. Riders see this only for orders they are delivering.</li>
    <li><strong>Service providers</strong> who help us run {SITE.name}: payments (Paystack), email delivery (Resend), sign-in (Google), and secure hosting and databases. They may only use your information to provide their service to us. Some store data on servers outside Ghana; when that happens we make sure your information stays protected as Act 843 requires.</li>
    <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, when the law requires it or to protect someone's safety.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong></p>

  <h2 id="location">Your location</h2>
  <p>
    If you allow it, we use your device's location to check that you are inside one of our delivery towns, to suggest
    your town and to help your rider find you. We only read your location while you are using the app, when you tap
    "Allow location" or "Use my location". You can say no and choose your area yourself, and you can turn location off
    at any time in your phone or browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="storage">Cookies and device storage</h2>
  <p>We store a few small pieces of information on your device so the app works:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>whether you are signed in;</li>
    <li>your chosen delivery area;</li>
    <li>the orders placed from this device, so you can see them without signing in;</li>
    <li>your bag and your favourites;</li>
    <li>whether you have seen the welcome screens;</li>
    <li>a random visitor number used to count visits.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use advertising cookies. Clearing your browser or app data removes this information from your device.</p>

  <h2 id="keep">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Order and payment records: as long as tax and accounting law requires.</li>
    <li>Your account: until you ask us to delete it. Some order records may need to be kept after that for legal reasons.</li>
    <li>Rider and restaurant documents: while the partner account is active, and for a limited time afterwards to deal with any complaints or legal claims.</li>
    <li>Usage information: in summary form only after 12 months.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security">Keeping it safe</h2>
  <p>
    We use encrypted connections, scrambled passwords, limited staff access and sign-in lockouts after repeated failed
    attempts. No system is perfectly secure, so please keep your email account and sign-in codes to yourself. We will never ask for
    your sign-in code, Mobile Money PIN or card PIN.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843), you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>ask us to correct information that is wrong;</li>
    <li>ask us to delete your information or your account;</li>
    <li>object to us using your information for marketing;</li>
    <li>complain to the Data Protection Commission of Ghana if you are unhappy with how we handle your information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To use any of these rights, contact us using the details below. We may ask you to confirm your phone number first.</p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    You must be 18 or older to create an account. We do not knowingly collect information from children. If you think a
    child has given us their information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the service grows. We will show the new date at the top and, for important changes,
    tell you in the app before they take effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Phone: <a href={`tel:${SITE.supportPhone}`}>{prettyPhone(SITE.supportPhone)}</a></li>
    <li>Support chat: <a href="/help/chat">chat with us in the app</a></li>
    <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a></li>
    <li>Post: {SITE.legalName}, {SITE.address}</li>
  </ul>
</LegalPage>
